00:12:34,041 --> 00:12:37,044
Now this isn’t about desserts or playlists.

255
00:12:37,044 --> 00:12:42,299
This is about preserving what makes us uniquely, messily and gloriously human.

256
00:12:42,299 --> 00:12:45,093
It’s your random passion for E.T. memorabilia,

257
00:12:45,093 --> 00:12:47,221
your weird detour into geocaching,

258
00:12:47,221 --> 00:12:49,973
or your stubborn preference for a stick-shift car.

259
00:12:49,973 --> 00:12:51,391
(Laughter)

260
00:12:51,391 --> 00:12:55,020
It’s about all the contradictions that AI can’t quite explain

261
00:12:55,020 --> 00:12:59,983
and the beauty of us being just a little weird once in a while.

262
00:12:59,983 --> 00:13:03,487
And if we believe that human complexity is worth preserving,

263
00:13:03,487 --> 00:13:05,614
then the time to act is now.

264
00:13:05,614 --> 00:13:09,701
Because we're at this inflection point where AI is no longer just recommending

265
00:13:09,701 --> 00:13:12,371
but starting to act on our behalf.

266
00:13:12,371 --> 00:13:15,707
It's choosing, not suggesting.

267
00:13:15,707 --> 00:13:19,545
And that's where the stakes become really existential.

268
00:13:19,545 --> 00:13:22,923
So next time AI offers you pralines and cream,

269
00:13:22,923 --> 00:13:24,341
maybe say no

270
00:13:24,341 --> 00:13:28,804
and ask it to help you go wild and reckless instead.

271
00:13:28,804 --> 00:13:29,972
Thank you.

272
00:13:29,972 --> 00:13:33,972
(Applause)
